      "message": "The addition `src_stride_yuy2 + 3` and similar additions are performed using the `int` type can potentially overflow. Since these functions return void, I cannot check for a big `src_stride_yuy2` and return -1.\n\nI can, however, add `ptrdiff_t` casts to these additions, for example,\n\n```\n    dst_v[0] \u003d (src_yuy2[3] + src_yuy2[(ptrdiff_t)src_stride_yuy2 + 3] + 1) \u003e\u003e 1;\n```\n\nWould you like me to do that instead?\n\nNote: I chose the current fix because the code looks nicer:\n\n```\n    dst_v[0] \u003d (src_yuy2[3] + src_yuy2_next[3] + 1) \u003e\u003e 1;\n```",
